      "A 12 mph top speed against the 95T’s 14",
      "A DC home drive, not the 95T’s club AC motor",
      "Published warranty terms differ between sources; check the current terms before buying",
    ],
    bottomLine: "The nearest new machine on Amazon to a 95T’s deck and rating, for less than a remanufactured one; it gives up the club drive and 2 mph of top speed.",
    description: "The 95T is sold remanufactured by specialist dealers, not on Amazon. The closest new treadmill we found there is SOLE’s TT8, its light-commercial model. The Amazon listing gives a 4.0 HP motor, a 22 by 60-inch running surface, a 0.5 to 12 mph speed range, an incline and decline range of -6 to 15 and a 15.6-inch touch screen, with programs including Hill, Fat Burn, HIIT, 10K and heart-rate control, and SOLE’s own site adds a non-folding frame and a 400 lb user capacity. That matches the 95T’s deck and rating on paper, and adds decline. What it does not match is the club drive: SOLE does not describe it as an AC motor, and it stops at 12 mph. It weighs more than 300 lb, so place it once. Published warranty terms differ: one SOLE comparison page gives lifetime frame and motor cover with two years on parts and one on labour, while other sources describe longer terms, so confirm them with SOLE. Amazon showed it at about $2,500 on 6 November 2026.",
  },
  {
    id: "life-fitness-t3",
    name: "Life Fitness T3",
    brand: "Life Fitness",
    category: "Amazon Alternative to the 95Ti: Life Fitness’s Compact Home Treadmill",
    badge: "Amazon Alternative",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B006BE6HW4?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/41xQfD1DGZL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":500},
    reviewUrl: null,
    priceRange: "$3,499–$4,119",
    priceBounds: {"low":3499,"high":4119},
    specs: "20 x 60 in. deck · 0.5–12 mph · 0–15% incline · 350 lb capacity · non-folding",
    pros: [
      "A new Life Fitness treadmill with the same 20 by 60-inch deck as the 95Ti",
      "Lifetime frame, ten years on the motor and five on parts",
      "At 243 lb, far easier to move and place than a 431 lb 95Ti",
      "Runs on a household outlet rather than a dedicated 20-amp circuit",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A 350 lb capacity, below the 95Ti’s 400 lb",
      "A 12 mph top speed and a home drive rather than a club AC motor",
      "More than a remanufactured 95Ti at its lowest price, once the console is chosen",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For a buyer who wants a Life Fitness name and a 60-inch deck new, with a long motor warranty, rather than a remanufactured club machine.",
    description: "The 95Ti is sold remanufactured, not on Amazon. If what draws you to it is a Life Fitness treadmill with a 60-inch deck, the T3 is the one sold on Amazon. Life Fitness and a major US retailer agree on a 20 by 60-inch running surface, the same deck size as the 95Ti, 0.5 to 12 mph, incline from 0 to 15%, a 350 lb maximum user weight and a machine weight of 243 lb, and both list the warranty as lifetime on the frame, ten years on the motor, five years on parts and one year of labour; Life Fitness adds three years on the console. Against a 95Ti it gives up 50 lb of rated capacity and the club AC drive, and gains a full new-machine warranty, a much lighter frame and no need for a dedicated circuit. Life Fitness sells it with a choice of console, at $3,499 with the Go console or $4,119 with Track Connect 2.0 on 15 October.",
  },
  {
    id: "life-fitness-run-cx",
    name: "Life Fitness Run CX",
    brand: "Life Fitness",
    category: "New Life Fitness Home Treadmill at a Similar Price",
    badge: "Buy New Instead",
    amazonUrl: "https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0C6B3C6FV?tag=sktiger-20&linkCode=ll1",
    amazonLabel: "Check Price on Amazon",
    image: {"url":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31c6k3CSuYL._SL500_.jpg","width":500,"height":435},
    reviewUrl: "/life-fitness-run-cx-treadmill/",
    priceRange: "$3,919 at Life Fitness on 5 Nov 2026",
    priceBounds: {"low":3919,"high":3919},
    specs: "22 x 60 in. running surface · 3.0 HP continuous DC (6.0 HP peak) · 0.5-12 mph · 0-15% incline · 400 lb max user · non-folding",
    pros: [
      "Less than a remanufactured 95T with a Discover console, and new",
      "Lifetime frame and Lifespring cover, 10 years on the motor and 7 on parts",
      "The same 22 by 60-inch deck and 400 lb rating as the 95T",
      "Plugs into a normal household outlet; delivery and installation included",
    ],
    cons: [
      "A DC motor, not a club AC drive",
      "Top speed of 12 mph against the 95T’s 14",
      "Life Fitness quoted a delivery lead time of several weeks",
    ],
    bottomLine: "For most home buyers, the better use of $4,000 than a remanufactured 95T: similar deck and rating, a new machine and a long warranty.",
