        <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic">
          If you search for a Life Fitness 95T, you will find dozens of listings — "95T Inspire", "95T Discover SE
          inc WiFi", "95Ti remanufactured" — and no way to buy one new from Life Fitness's US catalogue, which marks
          the Elevation Series treadmill as discontinued and points to the Integrity+ as its replacement. These
          are club treadmills built for a gym floor, and that is the attraction: a 4 HP AC drive, a 22 by 60-inch
          deck and a 400 lb rating for around $4,000 remanufactured. This guide covers what the 95T and 95Ti are,
          how the console names fit together, what sellers were asking on 5 November 2026, and the checks that
          matter when you buy a ten-year-old gym machine for a house.
        </p>

        <div id="short-answer" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">1. Can You Still Buy a Life Fitness 95T? The Short Answer</h2>
<p>
            <strong>Only remanufactured or used, in practice. Life Fitness's US catalogue marks the Elevation Series
            (95T) treadmill discontinued, and the 95Ti is older still. A remanufactured 95T at about $4,100 to
            $5,000, or a 95Ti from about $2,600, from a seller who gives a written warranty, is a fair way to get a
            club treadmill — if you have a dedicated 20-amp circuit. For similar money, a new Life Fitness Run CX
            is the simpler buy.</strong>
          </p>
          <p>
            On 5 November 2026 Life Fitness's US catalogue page for the Elevation Series treadmill carried the
            heading "Product Discontinued" and pointed to the Integrity+ treadmill as its replacement. Oddly, Life
            Fitness's separate Facility Shop for business customers still listed an Elevation Series treadmill
            with the Discover SE3 HD console at $16,999, available only with a business account. For a home buyer,
            the 95T is a remanufactured purchase.
          </p>
          <p>
            That is not a bad thing. These were among the most common club treadmills in the US, so there are
            plenty of them, and specialist remanufacturers strip them down, replace wear parts and sell them with
            their own warranties. On the day we checked, Fitness Superstore listed remanufactured 95Ts from $4,099
            and GymStore a 95Ti at $2,599. We have not tested any of them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="what-is-95t" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">2. 95T, 95Ti, Elevation, Inspire, Discover: What the Names Mean</h2>
<p>
            Life Fitness's naming confuses most buyers, because the treadmill and its console are named
            separately and sellers combine them freely.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>95Ti</strong> is the older club treadmill, with a 20-inch-wide belt and an LED console.
            Fitness Superstore says it was known as the "Silver Bullet". GymStore notes that a 95Ti was used for
            a 24-hour treadmill distance record of 153.76 miles by Christopher Bergland.</li>
            <li><strong>95T</strong> is the Elevation Series treadmill that followed it, with a 22-inch-wide deck,
            the DX3 belt and deck system and a range of interchangeable consoles.</li>
            <li><strong>Elevation Series</strong> is the product family name for the 95T and its matching bikes
            and cross-trainers.</li>
            <li><strong>Achieve, Inspire, Engage, Discover SI, Discover SE, Discover SE3 and SE3 HD</strong> are
            console names. A "95T Inspire" is a 95T base with the Inspire console; a "95T Discover SE" is the
            same base with the Discover SE touchscreen.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            So a listing for a "Life Fitness 95T Discover SE treadmill inc WiFi" — a phrasing used by UK sellers,
            where "inc" means "including" — is a 95T Elevation base with a Discover SE touchscreen console that
            has network connectivity. The running hardware is the same across every 95T console; what changes is
            the screen, the programs, the entertainment and the price.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What replaced it</h3>
          <p>
            Life Fitness names the <a href="/life-fitness-integrity-series-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Integrity+ treadmill</a>
            as the Elevation Series' replacement, and its US page also highlighted the Aspire and the HD Tread.
            For home buyers Life Fitness's current club-grade option is the
            <a href="/life-fitness-club-series-plus-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Club Series+</a>.
            Our <a href="/life-fitness/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Life Fitness brand guide</a> covers
            the whole range.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="specs" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">3. Life Fitness 95T and 95Ti Specifications</h2>
<p>
            The table gives the figures Life Fitness and sellers agree on, with conflicts noted. The 95T's figures
            are the same whichever console is fitted, apart from machine weight.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[560px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4"></th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">95T (Elevation Series)</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">95Ti</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Motor</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4.0 HP AC (8.0 HP peak), MagnaDrive</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">4.0 HP AC, MagnaDrive</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Running surface</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">22 x 60 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">20 x 60 in. belt</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Speed</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0.5-14 mph</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0.5-12 or 0.5-14 mph (sellers differ)</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Incline</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0-15%</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">0-15%</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Max user</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">400 lb</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">400 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Machine weight</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">442-444 lb (by console)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">431 lb</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Footprint (L x W)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">80 x 37 in.</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">83 x 37 in.</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Power</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Dedicated 120 V, 20 A circuit</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Dedicated 20 A circuit, NEMA 5-20</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <p>
            The 95T's figures come from Life Fitness's own catalogue page and match Fitness Superstore's
            listings. The 95Ti's come from Fitness Superstore and GymStore, which agree on everything except top
            speed. The 12 mph figure may reflect an older software setting or simply a listing error; ask the
            seller to show the unit reaching its top speed, or to confirm it in writing.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What those figures mean at home</h3>
          <p>
            A 4 HP continuous AC drive is built for a gym where the treadmill runs most of the day. In a home it
            is overbuilt, which is the point: it should run quietly at any speed for years. The 60-inch deck suits
            <a href="/best-treadmills-for-tall-runners/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>tall runners</a> and fast intervals, and 400 lb is a higher rating than most home treadmills. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-horsepower-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill horsepower guide</a>
            explains why AC and DC ratings are not directly comparable.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="consoles" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">4. The 95T Consoles Compared</h2>
<p>
            The console is what most separates one 95T listing from another, and what most affects its price and
            long-term usefulness.
          </p>
          <div class="not-prose overflow-x-auto my-8"><table class="min-w-[560px] w-full text-sm border-collapse">
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Console</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">What it is</th>
                <th class="text-left font-black text-gray-900 border-b border-gray-200 py-2 pr-4">Fitness Superstore, 5 Nov 2026</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Achieve</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Basic LED display, core programs</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,099</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Inspire</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">LED display with a fuller program set (fitness tests, terrain courses)</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,099</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Engage</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Upgraded display with more programs and languages</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,199</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Discover SI</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">10 in. touchscreen with internet connectivity and Bluetooth</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,199</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Discover SE</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Touchscreen with entertainment, Bluetooth and network features</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Listing not available on the day</td></tr>
              <tr><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">Discover SE3</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">19 in. touchscreen, TV tuner, device charging</td><td class="border-b border-gray-100 py-2 pr-4 text-gray-700">$4,999</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table></div>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Inspire: the sensible choice</h3>
          <p>
            The 95T Inspire is one of the most searched-for versions, and for a home it makes sense. Fitness
            Superstore's listing gives it a long program list — manual, hill, heart-rate, terrain courses, military
            fitness tests, 5K and 10K training and goal workouts — and a full set of readouts, with nothing that
            depends on a network or a subscription. It was the cheapest 95T Fitness Superstore listed on the day,
            tied with the Achieve.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Discover SE, SI and SE3: pay only if it all works</h3>
          <p>
            The Discover consoles are touchscreens built for gym members: TV, apps, internet browsing and, on
            some, logging workouts to Life Fitness accounts. Fitness Superstore says Bluetooth hardware ships in
            all Discover SE and SI consoles, and that on the SE, SE3 and SE3 HD standard TV works through a coax
            connector, while IPTV and other options must be bought, installed and configured by Life Fitness
            technicians. Listings that advertise "WiFi" mean the console can connect to a network, not that every
            service it was designed for still works in a house. Before paying $800 or more over an Inspire, ask the
            seller to show the specific apps you want running on the unit you are buying.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">The 95Ti console</h3>
          <p>
            The 95Ti uses an LED dot-matrix and alphanumeric display with a long list of programs, including heart
            rate, hill, interval and military fitness tests, according to GymStore. It has the least to go wrong of
            any of these consoles.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="models" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">5. Remanufactured Prices, and the New Alternative</h2>
<p>
            Remanufactured prices are what sellers asked on 5 November 2026, before freight: Fitness Superstore
            listed 95Ts at $4,099 (Achieve and Inspire consoles), $4,199 (Engage and Discover SI) and $4,999
            (Discover SE3), each with a year of parts and on-site labour, and remanufactured 95Tis ran from $2,599
            plus $699 shipping at GymStore to $3,799 at Fitness Superstore. The 95T and 95Ti are sold through
            remanufacturers and dealers, not on Amazon US, so the cards below show the nearest new alternatives
            sold there: the Sole TT8 for the 95T's 22 by 60-inch deck and 400 lb rating, Life Fitness's own T3 in
            place of the 95Ti, and the Life Fitness Run CX we would compare both with.
          </p>
          <p>
            Other listings in search results suggest a similar range: Keystone Fitness in Canada showed
            refurbished 95T Discover units at $3,999 to $4,449 (currency not stated), and SGroup Fitness listed a
            95T Inspire as out of stock. Prices for private sales on local marketplaces are often far lower, but
            come with no warranty and no inspection; our
            <a href="/where-to-buy-a-used-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">guide to where to buy a used treadmill</a>
            compares the options.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

