      <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">
        <div id="buying-remanufactured" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">6. How to Buy a Remanufactured 95T or 95Ti</h2>
<h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Know what "remanufactured" includes</h3>
          <p>
            A remanufactured treadmill should have been stripped down, cleaned, fitted with new wear parts and
            tested. Fitness Superstore describes a remanufacturing process on each listing; ask any seller for the
            list of parts replaced on your unit — belt, deck, rollers, bearings, <a href="/treadmill-motor-brushes/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium" data-autolink>motor brushes</a> if applicable — and
            get it in writing. "Refurbished" and "serviced" can mean much less. Our
            <a href="/refurbished-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">refurbished treadmills guide</a>
            explains the grades.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Warranty</h3>
          <p>
            The warranty comes from the seller, not Life Fitness. Fitness Superstore's standard term on these
            machines was one year of parts and on-site labour, with paid extensions up to five years in residential
            and commercial versions; GymStore offered six months or a year of additional cover. A seller who will
            not put a warranty in writing is selling as-is.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Freight and delivery</h3>
          <p>
            These machines weigh more than 430 lb. GymStore charged a fixed $699 for shipping on its 95Ti, and
            Fitness Superstore offered delivery options including room-of-choice and stair carry at extra cost,
            shipping the machine mostly assembled with the arms removed. Add delivery to the price before
            comparing sellers, and measure doorways and stairs. Our
            <a href="/treadmill-delivery-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">treadmill delivery guide</a>
            covers what to arrange.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">What to inspect</h3>
          <ul>
            <li>Run it at your normal speeds and through the full incline range, listening for motor, roller
            and incline-motor noise.</li>
            <li>Check the belt edges and ask whether the deck was flipped or replaced; the DX3 system on the 95T
            uses a lubricant-infused belt.</li>
            <li>On a touchscreen console, test every feature you are paying for.</li>
            <li>Ask for the serial number, so you can check its age and confirm it is not covered by a recall.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Our <a href="/used-treadmill-buying-checklist/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">used treadmill checklist</a>
            has the full list.
          </p>
          <h3 class="text-xl font-bold text-gray-900 mt-8 mb-3">Recalls</h3>
          <p>
            We searched the US Consumer Product Safety Commission's recall database for Life Fitness on
            5 November 2026. A 2003 recall-to-repair program covered specific serial ranges of the Life Fitness
            9000HR, 8500 and T9i treadmills, and a 2018 recall covered the PowerMill climber for a fire hazard.
            Neither involves the 95T or 95Ti.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="home-install" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">7. Putting a 95T in Your Home</h2>
<p>
            The 95T and 95Ti are gym machines, and they bring gym requirements into a house.
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>A dedicated 20-amp circuit.</strong> Life Fitness lists a dedicated 120 V, 20 A circuit
            for the 95T, and sellers list the same for the 95Ti with a NEMA 5-20 plug. Most household outlets are
            on shared 15-amp circuits; an electrician fitting a new circuit and 20-amp outlet is part of the cost.</li>
            <li><strong>Space.</strong> The 95T is 80 inches long and 37 wide, the 95Ti 83 by 37, and both stand
            about 62 to 64 inches high. Add safety clearance behind and to the sides.</li>
            <li><strong>Floor.</strong> At over 430 lb plus a runner, put it on a solid floor and a heavy mat, and
            think twice about an upper floor in an older house.</li>
          </ul>
          <p>
            Our <a href="/gym-treadmill-for-home/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">guide to putting a gym treadmill in a home</a>
            covers circuits, floors and access routes in detail, and our
            <a href="/commercial-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">commercial treadmills</a> guide
            compares other club brands.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div id="alternatives" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">8. Remanufactured 95T or New Life Fitness?</h2>
<p>
            For about $4,000, a remanufactured 95T Inspire gets you a club AC drive, a 22 by 60-inch deck, 14 mph
            and a 400 lb rating, with a year of seller's warranty. On 5 November 2026 the new
            <a href="/life-fitness-run-cx-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Life Fitness Run CX</a>
            was $3,919 with a lifetime frame warranty, 10 years on the motor, 7 on parts, delivery and installation,
            and no 20-amp circuit. For most home users that is the better buy. The 95T wins if you want a true club
            treadmill, will run fast or for many hours a week, or can buy one well below $4,000.
          </p>
          <p>
            Other club treadmills sold remanufactured in the same price range include the
            <a href="/cybex-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Cybex 770T and R Series</a>, also now
            under Life Fitness's ownership, and machines from
            <a href="/precor-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Precor</a> and
            <a href="/star-trac-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">Star Trac</a>. The same buying rules
            apply. If you are still deciding between new and used at all, our
            <a href="/new-vs-used-treadmill/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">new vs. used treadmill guide</a>
            sets out when each makes sense.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- FAQ -->
        <div id="faq" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">9. Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
          <div class="space-y-6">
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is the Life Fitness 95T discontinued?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Yes. On 5 November 2026 Life Fitness’s US catalogue page for the Elevation Series treadmill, the 95T, was headed "Product Discontinued" and named the Integrity+ as its replacement. Life Fitness’s business-only Facility Shop still listed one with the SE3 HD console at $16,999. Home buyers find the 95T remanufactured or used.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How much is a remanufactured Life Fitness 95T?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                On 5 November 2026 Fitness Superstore listed remanufactured 95Ts at $4,099 with the Achieve or Inspire console, $4,199 with the Engage or Discover SI and $4,999 with the Discover SE3, each with a one-year parts and on-site labour warranty. Freight is extra and prices change often.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the difference between the Life Fitness 95T and 95Ti?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                The 95Ti is the older model, with a 20-inch-wide belt and an LED console. The 95T is the Elevation Series treadmill that followed, with a 22 by 60-inch deck, the DX3 belt and deck system and a choice of consoles. Both have 4 HP AC motors, 15% incline and 400 lb ratings.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What are the Life Fitness 95T specs?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Life Fitness lists a 4 HP (8.0 HP peak) AC motor with MagnaDrive controller, a 22 by 60-inch running surface, 0.5 to 14 mph, 15% incline, a 400 lb maximum user and a dedicated 120 V, 20 A circuit. Remanufacturer listings agree and give an 80 by 37-inch footprint and 442 to 444 lb depending on the console.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What is the Life Fitness 95T Inspire?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It is the 95T Elevation Series treadmill fitted with the Inspire console, a display with a long program list including terrain courses, heart-rate workouts and fitness tests, and no reliance on a network. Fitness Superstore listed a remanufactured 95T Inspire at $4,099 on 5 November 2026.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What does "95T Discover SE inc WiFi" mean?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It describes a 95T Elevation treadmill with the Discover SE touchscreen console and network connectivity; "inc" is UK shorthand for "including". The running hardware is the same as any 95T. Before paying extra, check which of the console’s apps and TV features still work on the unit you are buying.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-gray-50 rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100">
              <h3 class="font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Is a remanufactured Life Fitness 95Ti worth buying?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                It can be at $2,600 to $3,800 from a remanufacturer with a written warranty, if you have a dedicated 20-amp circuit. Sellers disagree on its top speed, 12 or 14 mph, so confirm it on the unit. For about $3,900, a new Life Fitness Run CX is the simpler choice for most homes.
              </p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Common Mistakes -->
        <div class="mt-16">
          <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6">Common Mistakes Buying a Used Life Fitness 95T</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">A remanufactured 95T can be excellent value. These are the ways buyers end up paying more for less.</p>
          <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Paying for a touchscreen that no longer does much</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Discover consoles add up to $900 over an Inspire on the listings we saw, but their TV, app and network features were designed for gyms in the 2010s. Pay for one only after seeing the features you want working on that unit.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Forgetting the 20-amp circuit</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Life Fitness lists a dedicated 120 V, 20 A circuit for the 95T. Running it on a shared 15-amp household circuit risks tripped breakers and electronics faults. Price the electrician in before you compare it with a new home treadmill.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Comparing prices without freight</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">A 95Ti at $2,599 plus $699 shipping costs nearly as much as a 95T elsewhere with cheaper delivery. Ask every seller for a delivered price, including stairs or room-of-choice placement if you need it.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying without a written warranty</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">No Life Fitness warranty transfers to a second-hand buyer. The remanufacturer’s warranty is all you have, so get its length, what it covers and who does on-site labour in writing, along with the list of replaced parts.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

