        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">The Life Fitness 95T (Elevation Series) and older 95Ti are discontinued club
          treadmills, sold remanufactured: about $4,100 to $5,000 for a 95T and from about $2,600 for a 95Ti on
          5 November 2026.</strong> Both have 4 HP AC drives, 15% incline and 400 lb ratings; the 95T adds a
          22 by 60-inch deck. Buy from a remanufacturer with a written warranty and a parts list, choose the
          Inspire console unless you will really use a touchscreen, and have a dedicated 20-amp circuit ready.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            For most home buyers, the new
          <a href="/life-fitness-run-cx-treadmill/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">Life Fitness Run CX</a>
